# OpenRAL — example reasoner LLM configurations
#
# Pick ONE of the blocks below, copy to `.env` (gitignored), and
# `source .env` before `ros2 run openral_reasoner_ros reasoner_node` or
# any sim run that activates the S2 reasoner. `openral doctor` will report
# what's missing if any required variable is unset.
#
# CLAUDE.md §1.4 — the open core has no default LLM. Explicit beats
# implicit; you must pick one here.
#
# Selection is model-first (ADR-0088): OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL says WHICH
# model, OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT says WHERE it runs. A curated model
# (claude-opus-4-8 / gpt-5.5 / gpt-5.6 / cosmos3-edge) needs no endpoint —
# the registry has its default. Anything else is an *uncurated* model id:
# it needs an endpoint, and the reasoner logs a `reasoner.model.uncurated`
# warning (untested for robotics tool calling).
#
# OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT takes a NAMED endpoint — anthropic, openrouter,
# gemini, xai, deepseek, huggingface, ollama, vllm — or a bare URL. A name
# carries its own base URL, dialect, auth posture and cold-start timeout, so
# OPENRAL_REASONER_DIALECT is needed only for a bare URL.
#
# The provider-first OPENRAL_REASONER_LLM_* contract was removed in 0.3.0.
# Migration table: packages/openral_reasoner_ros/README.md.

# ── Option 1: paid baseline (curated Claude) ─────────────────────────
# Native tool use. One-time: `uv add anthropic --package openral-reasoner`
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Option 2: curated OpenRouter models ──────────────────────────────
# gpt-5.5 / gpt-5.6 resolve to OpenRouter by default.
# One-time: `uv add openai --package openral-reasoner`
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=gpt-5.5
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# ── Option 3: local baseline (Ollama + Qwen3 8B) ─────────────────────
# Setup: `just bootstrap-ollama`
# One-time: `uv add openai --package openral-reasoner`
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT=ollama

# ── Option 4: on-device physical-AI planner (curated Cosmos 3) ───────
# Managed local vLLM sidecar, auto-started on the first tick.
# Disable the spawn with OPENRAL_COSMOS3_AUTOSTART=0.
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=cosmos3-edge

# ── Uncurated model on a named vendor endpoint ───────────────────────
# Any model the vendor serves, via its own OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# One-time: `uv add openai --package openral-reasoner`
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT=gemini    # or: xai / deepseek /
#                                            #     openrouter / huggingface
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_API_KEY=...

# ── Self-hosted vLLM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `vllm serve <model>` on the loopback default (:8000, no auth).
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=qwen2.5-7b-instruct
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT=vllm

# ── Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (bare URL) ──────────────────
# Nothing can classify a bare URL, so declare the dialect explicitly.
#
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_MODEL=qwen2.5-7b-instruct
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_ENDPOINT=http://gpu-box.internal:8001/v1
# export OPENRAL_REASONER_DIALECT=openai
